# EXPERIMENTS.md

Record at least ten real experiments. Each entry must contain a hypothesis, one controlled change, actual result/evidence, and decision. Do not pre-fill success claims.

## Suggested experiment matrix

| ID | Question | Controlled comparison | Evidence to collect |
|---|---|---|---|
| E01 | Does a character reference improve identity consistency? | With reference vs without | Chosen images, evaluation notes |
| E02 | Does a fixed style block improve visual continuity? | Fixed vs varied style wording | Shot comparison |
| E03 | How much does seed affect image composition? | Several seeds, same prompt | Seeds and outputs |
| E04 | Which prompt length gives clearer images? | Concise vs detailed | Output comparison |
| E05 | Which motion prompt is more stable? | Gentle vs complex movement | Clip artifacts and latency |
| E06 | What resolution is practical on allocated Colab GPU? | Draft vs final resolution | GPU memory/time, quality |
| E07 | Which Amharic TTS style sounds most natural? | Calm vs warm/neutral direction | Native-speaker feedback |
| E08 | Is narration easier to correct by shot? | One long file vs segmented lines | Retake time and alignment |
| E09 | Which original score best supports the film? | Three score candidates | Listening decision and rationale |
| E10 | Does music ducking improve intelligibility? | Ducking on vs off | Listening / measured levels |
| E11 | Is still animation an acceptable fallback? | Wan clip vs pan/zoom | Quality, time, resource use |
| E12 | Which crop preserves composition in both ratios? | Center-safe vs alternative framing | Vertical/horizontal review |

## Experiment record template

### E## — [TITLE]
- Date/time:
- Hypothesis:
- Controlled change (change one main variable):
- Fixed variables / seed:
- Model and parameters:
- Evidence/output paths:
- Latency / GPU minutes / cost estimate:
- Actual result:
- Decision and why:
